-- חוזר לבעלויות תשפ"ד/1 (18.7.2023): העסקת עו"ה, עובדי בעלות, בבתי ספר יסודיים
-- מוכרים שאינם רשמיים שהם בבעלות רשת מעיין החינוך התורני ורשת החינוך העצמאי,
-- בהתאם לרפורמת אופק חדש בשנה"ל תשפ"ד.
-- Bringing the primary schools of the two networks into Ofek Hadash from
-- תשפ"ד: who does what and by when, who joins, the work week, part-time and
-- over-100% employment, mothers' and age hours, principals and deputies,
-- school-activity hours, leaving the reform, seniority, promotion,
-- counselors, grade determination and role bonuses, trip escort pay,
-- salary advances, the attendance clock, and the annexes (the owner's
-- commitment, the forms, and the salary-conversion method).

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

-- Time in this file's regulative rules is counted in DAYS from 18 July 2023
-- (day 0), the circular's date.
`30 July 2023`     MEANS 12
`1 September 2023` MEANS 45
`31 August 2024`   MEANS 410

-- Two money helpers for the annex's worked examples: to the agora by
-- truncation, and to the agora rounded half up (amounts here are positive).
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `truncated to the agora` x IS TRUNC x 2

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `rounded to the agora` x IS TRUNC (x PLUS 0.005) 2

§ `חוזר לבעלויות תשפ"ד/1`

-- akn:preamble The letterhead, date, reference number, circular number, addressees (the owners of the regular primary schools of the Maayan HaChinuch HaTorani and HaChinuch HaAtzmai networks), greeting and subject line; no rule.

DECLARE `network` IS ONE OF
    `Maayan HaChinuch HaTorani`
    `HaChinuch HaAtzmai`
    `another owner`

@desc A school, as far as this circular asks about one.
DECLARE `tashpad 1 school` HAS
    `owner network`                 IS A `network`
    `recognized unofficial primary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc a recognized unofficial (מוכר שאינו רשמי) primary school of the regular education system
    `share of teachers eligible and wishing to join` IS A NUMBER @desc the share of its teaching employees who meet the joining conditions (education, training, position) and wish to join

DECLARE `role` IS ONE OF
    `teacher`
    `principal`
    `first deputy principal`
    `second or later deputy principal`
    `educational counselor`

@desc A teaching employee of the owner, as far as this circular asks about one.
DECLARE `tashpad 1 teacher` HAS
    `teacher role`                   IS A `role`
    `academic`                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc holds an academic degree, or a salary grade the Ministry's teaching-staff division approved as equivalent to an academic one
    `certified to teach`             IS A BOOLEAN @desc holds a teaching certificate or certification
    `prior teaching years recognized` IS A NUMBER @desc years of actual teaching recognized before (from a non-State employer or in State service), not counting an internship year or teaching in IDF or national service
    `teaching seniority`             IS A NUMBER  @desc years of teaching seniority
    `position fraction`              IS A NUMBER  @desc the share of a full position held (1 = 100%)
    `is an intern`                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc in the internship (סטאז') year
    `approved as an exception`       IS A BOOLEAN @desc the teaching-staff division's exceptions committee approved joining without a teaching certificate (3.2.1)
    `age`                            IS A NUMBER  @desc age, determined as before the reform (8.1)

§§ `1 מבוא`

-- akn:art_1/p1 akn:art_1/p2 akn:art_1/p3 akn:art_1/p4 The background: section 4 of government decision 511 (printed "14.5.3023") directs the Minister to amend regulation 3(א)(6) of the recognized-institutions regulations so teachers' salaries in recognized unofficial schools follow the rates and rules of official Ofek Hadash schools, as the special-education circular for תשפ"ב applied them; no rule of this circular's own.
-- akn:art_1/p5 akn:art_1/p6 The Ministry implements the decision gradually; in תשפ"ה it extends to further owners in recognized unofficial education; no rule for תשפ"ד.

-- ¶7: the circular sets the instructions for the teaching employees these
-- owners employ who teach in their recognized unofficial primary schools,
-- for תשפ"ד.
@ref akn:art_1/p7
GIVEN s IS A `tashpad 1 school`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the circular covers` s IF
        s's `recognized unofficial primary`
    AND NOT (s's `owner network` EQUALS `another owner`)

§§ `2 תחומי אחריות ביישום הרפורמה`

-- akn:art_2 The heading of section 2; no rule.
-- akn:art_2__para_2-1 The heading "שלב ראשון" (stage one); no rule.
-- akn:art_2__para_2-1__hc_1 The heading "פעולות המתבצעות ע"י הבעלות" (the owner's actions); no rule.

DECLARE `tashpad 1 action` IS ONE OF
    `submit the commitment letter`
    `verify and update the teachers' data`
    `act by the employment-approval circular`
    `identify the teachers who meet the joining conditions`
    `employ by the Ofek Hadash terms`
    `guide teachers to open an online file`
    `set the timetable by the Ofek Hadash work week`
    `place every teacher in the placement system`
    `send the salary interface to the contractor`
    `pay by the determined grade and offset the advances`
    `set the Ofek Hadash grade`
    `update the teachers' data in the Ministry`
    `add the joining institutions to the Ministry's systems`
    `decide each teacher's joining`
    `report the teachers' updated data to the owner`
    `pay the Ofek Hadash advance` HAS `advance paid` IS A NUMBER
    `install an attendance clock`
    `report hours by the attendance clock`
    `report hours by hand`
    `pay and deduct by the attendance reports`
    `apply the Ofek Hadash agreement`

-- 2.1, owner 1: find the institutions in which 50% of the teaching
-- employees can enter Ofek Hadash by their education, training and
-- position, and wish to.
@ref akn:art_2__para_2-1__hc_1__subpara_1
GIVEN s IS A `tashpad 1 school`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the institution may join` s IF
        `the circular covers` s
    AND s's `share of teachers eligible and wishing to join` AT LEAST 0.5

-- 2.1, owner 2: until the regulations are amended, the owner signs a
-- commitment (annex א) to apply Ofek Hadash in its schools that choose it
-- and meet the threshold, and sends it by e-mail; the last day is 30.7.2023.
@ref akn:art_2__para_2-1__hc_1__subpara_2 akn:art_2__para_2-1__hc_1__subpara_2/p2 akn:art_2__para_2-1__hc_1__subpara_2/p3
GIVEN s IS A `tashpad 1 school`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `tashpad 1 action`
DECIDE `the commitment letter` s IS
    IF `the institution may join` s
    THEN PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
         MUST  `submit the commitment letter`
         WITHIN `30 July 2023`
         LEST BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "circular תשפ\"ד/1 2.1(2): the last day to send the commitment letter is 30.7.2023"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- 2.1, owner 3: the teaching-staff data report in the עוש"ר system lists the
-- teachers as reported. (א) the owner must make sure the data (academic and
-- pedagogic education, seniorities including IDF and national service,
-- in-service-training credits and double degree) are current, and have
-- them updated through the Haredi district; a contact person is suggested.
-- (ב) the steps follow the circular on employment approval. (ג) after
-- stage א, find the teachers who meet the joining conditions (section 3).
-- The text sets no deadline for these steps, so none has one.
@ref akn:art_2__para_2-1__hc_1__subpara_3 akn:art_2__para_2-1__hc_1__subpara_3__cls_a akn:art_2__para_2-1__hc_1__subpara_3__cls_b akn:art_2__para_2-1__hc_1__subpara_3__cls_c
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `tashpad 1 action`
DECIDE `the teachers' data are kept current` IS
    (PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
     MUST  `verify and update the teachers' data`
     LEST BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "circular תשפ\"ד/1 2.1(3)(א): the owner must make sure the teachers' data are current")
    RAND
    (PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
     MUST  `act by the employment-approval circular`
     LEST BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "circular תשפ\"ד/1 2.1(3)(ב): the steps follow the owners' circular on employment approval")
    RAND
    (PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
     MUST  `identify the teachers who meet the joining conditions`
     LEST BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "circular תשפ\"ד/1 2.1(3)(ג): after stage א, the teachers who meet the joining conditions are found")

-- 2.1, owner 4: the teachers who meet the joining conditions are employed
-- on Ofek Hadash's salary terms and work week, as updated by the October
-- 2022 agreement and before (section 4).
@ref akn:art_2__para_2-1__hc_1__subpara_4
GIVEN t IS A `tashpad 1 teacher`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `tashpad 1 action`
DECIDE `employment by the Ofek Hadash terms` t IS
    IF `joins Ofek Hadash` t
    THEN PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
         MUST  `employ by the Ofek Hadash terms`
         LEST BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "circular תשפ\"ד/1 2.1(4): a teacher who meets the joining conditions is employed on Ofek Hadash's terms"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- akn:art_2__para_2-1__hc_2 The heading "פעולת המתבצעות ע"י מנהל בית הספר" (the principal's actions); no rule.

-- 2.1, principal 1-3: guide teachers without a file to open an online
-- file; set the timetable of reform teachers by the Ofek Hadash work week
-- (section 4); place every teacher — in the reform or not — in the
-- placement system (משכית). The text sets no deadline for them.
@ref akn:art_2__para_2-1__hc_2__subpara_1 akn:art_2__para_2-1__hc_2__subpara_2 akn:art_2__para_2-1__hc_2__subpara_3
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `tashpad 1 action`
DECIDE `the principal's stage-one actions` IS
    (PARTY `the school principal` MUST `guide teachers to open an online file`)
    RAND
    (PARTY `the school principal` MUST `set the timetable by the Ofek Hadash work week`)
    RAND
    (PARTY `the school principal` MUST `place every teacher in the placement system`)

-- 2.2, owner 1: once the data are updated, the owner sends the contractor
-- (Unique) an interface of the salary it paid in the month requested; the
-- Ministry then sets each teacher's Ofek Hadash grade and converts the
-- salary. 2.2, owner 2: once the grade is set and reported back, the owner
-- pays by it from the joining date and offsets the salary advances.
-- The text sets no deadline for these steps.
-- F-2023-24_tashpad_01-b: the advances are said to be "כאמור בסעיף 15
-- להלן"; section 15 is the trip-escort bonus, and the advances are section 16.
@ref akn:art_2__para_2-2 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_1 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `tashpad 1 action`
DECIDE `stage two` IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    MUST  `send the salary interface to the contractor`
    HENCE (PARTY `the Ministry of Education`
           MUST  `set the Ofek Hadash grade`
           HENCE (PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
                  MUST  `pay by the determined grade and offset the advances`))

`the section 2.2 says the advances are in` MEANS 15
`the section the advances are in` MEANS 16
`the trip-escort section` MEANS 15

`2.2's reference to the advances points at the trip-escort section` MEANS
        `the section 2.2 says the advances are in` EQUALS `the trip-escort section`
    AND NOT (`the section 2.2 says the advances are in` EQUALS `the section the advances are in`)
#ASSERT `2.2's reference to the advances points at the trip-escort section`

-- 2.2 ¶2-¶9: the Ministry (1) updates the teachers' data; (2) adds the
-- joining institutions to its systems; (3) checks each teacher against the
-- joining conditions after the תשפ"ד position is reported; (4) sets the
-- grade of each teacher who joined; (5) reports the data back to the owner.
-- Only once the data are updated can the next step follow. No deadline is
-- stated.
@ref akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2/p2 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2/p3 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2/p4 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2/p5 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2/p6 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2/p7 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2/p8 akn:art_2__para_2-2__subpara_2/p9
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `tashpad 1 action`
DECIDE `the Ministry sets the grades` IS
    PARTY `the Ministry of Education`
    MUST  `update the teachers' data in the Ministry`
    HENCE (PARTY `the Ministry of Education`
           MUST  `add the joining institutions to the Ministry's systems`
           HENCE (PARTY `the Ministry of Education`
                  MUST  `decide each teacher's joining`
                  HENCE (PARTY `the Ministry of Education`
                         MUST  `set the Ofek Hadash grade`
                         HENCE (PARTY `the Ministry of Education`
                                MUST  `report the teachers' updated data to the owner`))))

§§ `3 תנאי ההצטרפות`

-- akn:art_3 The heading of section 3; no rule.
-- akn:art_3__para_3-1 The heading "הגדרות" (definitions); no rule.

-- 3.1.1 a new teaching employee: no years of actual teaching recognized
-- before (internship, IDF or national-service teaching aside). 3.1.2 an
-- existing one: entitled to recognition of years of actual teaching for
-- salary seniority.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-1__subpara_3-1-1
GIVEN t IS A `tashpad 1 teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a new teaching employee` t IF
    t's `prior teaching years recognized` EQUALS 0

@ref akn:art_3__para_3-1__subpara_3-1-2
GIVEN t IS A `tashpad 1 teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an existing teaching employee` t IF
    t's `prior teaching years recognized` GREATER THAN 0

-- akn:art_3__para_3-2 The heading of 3.2 (joining conditions of existing teaching employees); no rule.
-- akn:art_3__para_3-2__subpara_3-2-1 The heading "עו"ה קיימים אקדמאים" (existing academic teaching employees); no rule.

-- 3.2.1: an existing academic teacher in a joined institution joins if
-- certified to teach and employed at a third of a position or more.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-2__subpara_3-2-1/p2 akn:art_3__para_3-2__subpara_3-2-1/p3 akn:art_3__para_3-2__subpara_3-2-1/p4 akn:art_3__para_3-2__subpara_3-2-1/p5 akn:art_3__para_3-2__subpara_3-2-1/p6
GIVEN t IS A `tashpad 1 teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an existing academic meets the conditions` t IF
        t's `certified to teach`
    AND t's `position fraction` AT LEAST (1 DIVIDED BY 3)

-- 3.2.1 ¶7-¶8: one without a teaching certificate may apply, as an
-- exception, to the teaching-staff division's exceptions committee on the
-- form of annex ב, sent by the principal by e-mail.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-2__subpara_3-2-1/p7 akn:art_3__para_3-2__subpara_3-2-1/p8
GIVEN t IS A `tashpad 1 teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an uncertified academic joins as an exception` t IF
        NOT t's `certified to teach`
    AND t's `approved as an exception`

-- 3.2.1 ¶9-¶10: a teacher without a teaching certificate and with under 25
-- years of seniority cannot advance in grade until certified; the work and
-- part of the studies count towards promotion "as in section 12.2.2".
-- F-2023-24_tashpad_01-c: section 12.2 has no 12.2.2; the rule is 13.2.2.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-2__subpara_3-2-1/p9 akn:art_3__para_3-2__subpara_3-2-1/p10
GIVEN t IS A `tashpad 1 teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `barred from advancing until certified under 3.2.1` t IF
        NOT t's `certified to teach`
    AND t's `teaching seniority` LESS THAN 25

`the subsections section 12.2 has` MEANS EMPTY
`3.2.1's reference to 12.2.2 has no target` MEANS
    NOT elem "12.2.2" `the subsections section 12.2 has`
#ASSERT `3.2.1's reference to 12.2.2 has no target`

-- akn:art_3__para_3-3 The heading of 3.3 (existing non-academic teaching employees); no rule.

-- 3.3.1-3.3.2: an existing non-academic with 28 years or more is employed on
-- the reform's terms in any case; with fewer than 28, not.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-3__subpara_3-3-1 akn:art_3__para_3-3__subpara_3-3-2
GIVEN t IS A `tashpad 1 teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an existing non-academic joins` t IF
    t's `teaching seniority` AT LEAST 28

-- akn:art_3__para_3-4 The heading of 3.4 (joining new teaching employees); no rule.

DECLARE `salary table` IS ONE OF
    `the bachelor's degree table`
    `the master's degree table`
    `a table by education (senior, certified or uncertified)`
    `no table`

-- 3.4 ¶2-¶6: a new academic in a joined institution is placed at grade 1,
-- seniority 1: a BA in the BA table, an MA in the MA table, a doctorate in
-- the MA table with a 5% supplement on the combined salary.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-4/p2
`the starting grade of a new academic` MEANS 1
`the starting seniority of a new academic` MEANS 1

@ref akn:art_3__para_3-4/p3 akn:art_3__para_3-4/p4 akn:art_3__para_3-4/p5
GIVEN d IS A `degree`
GIVETH A `salary table`
DECIDE `the table a new academic is placed in` d IS
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN `bachelor's` THEN `the bachelor's degree table`
    WHEN `master's` THEN `the master's degree table`
    WHEN `doctorate` THEN `the master's degree table`
    WHEN `no degree` THEN `no table`

DECLARE `degree` IS ONE OF `bachelor's`, `master's`, `doctorate`, `no degree`

@ref akn:art_3__para_3-4/p6
GIVEN d IS A `degree`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the doctorate supplement rate` d IS
    IF d EQUALS `doctorate` THEN 0.05 ELSE 0

-- 3.4 ¶7: new non-academic teachers not entitled to an intern's salary
-- under sections 145-148 of the Ofek Hadash agreement are placed in the
-- salary tables by their education (senior, certified or uncertified).
-- F-2023-24_tashpad_01-n: the paragraph sits under "joining new teachers to
-- Ofek Hadash" and does not say whether these teachers join the reform;
-- senior/certified/uncertified are the pre-reform classes. The reading
-- adopted: they are not employed on the reform's terms (as 3.3.2 says of
-- existing non-academics), and are placed by education.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-4/p7
GIVEN t IS A `tashpad 1 teacher`
GIVETH A `salary table`
DECIDE `the table a new non-academic is placed in` t IS
    `a table by education (senior, certified or uncertified)`

-- The other reading: ¶7 is one of 3.4's rules for joining new teachers,
-- so a new non-academic joins and is placed on the reform's tables by
-- education.
GIVEN t IS A `tashpad 1 teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a new non-academic joins if 3.4 ¶7 is a joining rule` t IF
    `is a new teaching employee` t AND NOT t's `is an intern`

`3.4 ¶7 leaves open whether new non-academics join the reform` MEANS
    NOT (`a new non-academic joins if 3.4 ¶7 is a joining rule` `a new non-academic teacher`
         EQUALS `joins Ofek Hadash` `a new non-academic teacher`)
#ASSERT `3.4 ¶7 leaves open whether new non-academics join the reform`

-- akn:art_3__para_3-4_2 The heading of the second 3.4 (interns); no rule.

-- 3.4.1 (the second 3.4): in a joined school interns are employed only on
-- the reform's terms; the internship year counts only at a third of a
-- position or more.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-4_2__subpara_3-4-1
GIVEN t IS A `tashpad 1 teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the internship year is recognized` t IF
        t's `is an intern`
    AND t's `position fraction` AT LEAST (1 DIVIDED BY 3)

-- 3.4.2: the internship lasts at most two years, in which the intern must
-- complete a degree and a teaching certificate, or may not stay on the
-- reform's terms.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-4_2__subpara_3-4-2
`the longest internship in years` MEANS 2

GIVEN `years in internship` IS A NUMBER, `completed degree and certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an intern may stay on the reform's terms` `years in internship` `completed degree and certificate` IF
    `years in internship` AT MOST `the longest internship in years` OR `completed degree and certificate`

-- 3.4.3: the internship does not count for salary seniority or the minimum
-- period for promotion; it counts for tenure, the jubilee grant and
-- recuperation.
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-4_2__subpara_3-4-3
GIVEN p IS A `seniority purpose`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the internship counts for` p IF
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `salary seniority` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the minimum period for promotion` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

DECLARE `seniority purpose` IS ONE OF
    `salary seniority`
    `the minimum period for promotion`
    `tenure`
    `the jubilee grant`
    `recuperation`

-- akn:art_3__para_3-4_2__subpara_3-4-4 akn:art_3__para_3-4_2__subpara_3-4-4/p2 akn:art_3__para_3-4_2__subpara_3-4-4/p3 A link to the details of interns' evaluation; no rule.
-- akn:art_3__para_3-4_2__subpara_3-4-5 akn:art_3__para_3-4_2__subpara_3-4-5/p2 akn:art_3__para_3-4_2__subpara_3-4-5/p3 A link to the map of dimensions for evaluating interns; no rule.

-- Who joins Ofek Hadash in a joined institution, by 3.2-3.4.
GIVEN t IS A `tashpad 1 teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `joins Ofek Hadash` t IF
    BRANCH IF t's `is an intern` THEN TRUE
           IF `is a new teaching employee` t THEN t's `academic`
           IF t's `academic` THEN `an existing academic meets the conditions` t OR `an uncertified academic joins as an exception` t
           OTHERWISE `an existing non-academic joins` t

`a new non-academic teacher` MEANS
    `tashpad 1 teacher` WITH
        `teacher role`                    IS `teacher`
        `academic`                        IS FALSE
        `certified to teach`              IS TRUE
        `prior teaching years recognized` IS 0
        `teaching seniority`              IS 0
        `position fraction`               IS 0.8
        `is an intern`                    IS FALSE
        `approved as an exception`        IS FALSE
        `age`                             IS 25

-- akn:art_3__para_3-5 The heading of 3.5 (substitute teachers); no rule.

-- 3.5: a substitute employed in weekly hours (not single hours), in the
-- reform or not, is employed on the terms of the teacher replaced. A
-- substitute in single hours is not what 3.5 decides (NOTHING).
@ref akn:art_3__para_3-5/p2
GIVEN `employed in weekly hours` IS A BOOLEAN, `the replaced teacher is in the reform` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a substitute is on the reform's terms` `employed in weekly hours` `the replaced teacher is in the reform` IS
    IF `employed in weekly hours`
    THEN JUST `the replaced teacher is in the reform`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `4 מבנה שבוע העבודה למורים באופק חדש`

-- akn:art_4 The heading of section 4; no rule.
-- akn:art_4__para_4-1 The heading of 4.1 (a teacher in a primary school with grades 1-6, 1-8 or 1-9); no rule.

-- 4.1: a primary teacher whose base was kept at the junior-high base (24
-- hours a week), or a new teacher in an 8- or 9-year primary school in
-- grades 7-9, works by the primary teacher's week "as in section 4.3".
-- F-2023-24_tashpad_01-d: there is no 4.3 (nor the 4.3.1 that 4.2.2 and
-- 4.2.3 cite); the primary work week is 4.2.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-1/p2
GIVEN `base kept at the junior-high base` IS A BOOLEAN, `new teacher in grades 7-9 of a primary school` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `work week`
DECIDE `the week of a primary teacher under 4.1` `base kept at the junior-high base` `new teacher in grades 7-9 of a primary school` IS
    IF `base kept at the junior-high base` OR `new teacher in grades 7-9 of a primary school`
    THEN JUST `the primary teacher's week`
    ELSE NOTHING

`the subsections section 4 has` MEANS LIST "4.1", "4.2", "4.2.1", "4.2.2", "4.2.3", "4.2.4", "4.2.5"
`section 4 cites a 4.3 and a 4.3.1 it does not have` MEANS
    (NOT elem "4.3" `the subsections section 4 has`) AND (NOT elem "4.3.1" `the subsections section 4 has`)
#ASSERT `section 4 cites a 4.3 and a 4.3.1 it does not have`

-- akn:art_4__para_4-2 The heading of 4.2 (the work week of a primary teaching employee); no rule.

@desc A full-position weekly work structure, in hours.
DECLARE `work week` HAS
    `week total`      IS A NUMBER
    `week frontal`    IS A NUMBER
    `week individual` IS A NUMBER
    `week stay`       IS A NUMBER

-- 4.2.1-4.2.4: 36 hours: 26 frontal, 5 individual (groups of up to 5
-- pupils, content set by the principal under the Ministry's guidance), 5
-- stay hours at school.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-2__subpara_4-2-1 akn:art_4__para_4-2__subpara_4-2-2 akn:art_4__para_4-2__subpara_4-2-3 akn:art_4__para_4-2__subpara_4-2-4
`the primary teacher's week` MEANS `work week` WITH
    `week total`      IS 36
    `week frontal`    IS 26
    `week individual` IS 5
    `week stay`       IS 5

`the largest individual-hours group` MEANS 5

#ASSERT `the primary teacher's week`'s `week frontal` PLUS `the primary teacher's week`'s `week individual` PLUS `the primary teacher's week`'s `week stay` EQUALS `the primary teacher's week`'s `week total`

-- 4.2.4(1)-(2): of the stay hours, work meetings take up to 2 a week; the
-- rest go to preparing material and planning, meeting parents, and marking.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-2__subpara_4-2-4__cls_1 akn:art_4__para_4-2__subpara_4-2-4__cls_2 akn:art_4__para_4-2__subpara_4-2-4__cls_2/p2 akn:art_4__para_4-2__subpara_4-2-4__cls_2/p3 akn:art_4__para_4-2__subpara_4-2-4__cls_2/p4
@desc What a teacher does in the stay hours at school (4.2.4).
DECLARE `stay-hour activity` IS ONE OF
    `work meetings` @desc of the pedagogic council, with other teachers on shared pupils, of the subject teams, of the multi-professional teams, with outside bodies and the like
    `preparing learning materials and planning the teaching`
    `individual meetings with parents`
    `marking work and tests`

`the most stay hours for work meetings` MEANS 2

-- 4.2.5: an individual or stay hour is as long as a frontal hour by the
-- school's timetable; break time is not a stay hour.
@ref akn:art_4__para_4-2__subpara_4-2-5
GIVEN `minutes of a frontal hour` IS A NUMBER, `break minutes` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `minutes of a stay hour` `minutes of a frontal hour` `break minutes` IS
    `minutes of a frontal hour`

`a break counts as stay time` MEANS FALSE

-- akn:art_4/p1 akn:art_4/p2 akn:art_4/p3 A link to the detailed work-week table of a primary teaching employee; no rule.

§§ `5 העסקה בחלקיות משרה ברפורמה`

-- akn:art_5 The heading of section 5; no rule.

-- 5.1: no less than a third of a position. 5.2: a new teacher (not an
-- intern) at least 70%, and from 1.9.2024 at least 80%; an intern and an
-- existing teacher at least a third, so as to earn a year of seniority.
@ref akn:art_5__para_5-1 akn:art_5__para_5-2 akn:art_5__para_5-2/p2
GIVEN t IS A `tashpad 1 teacher`, `from 1.9.2024` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the minimum position` t `from 1.9.2024` IS
    IF `is a new teaching employee` t AND NOT t's `is an intern`
    THEN IF `from 1.9.2024` THEN 0.8 ELSE 0.7
    ELSE 1 DIVIDED BY 3

-- 5.3: a part-time position is cut proportionally across frontal,
-- individual and stay hours.
@ref akn:art_5__para_5-3
GIVEN w IS A `work week`, f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `work week`
DECIDE `the part-time week` w f IS
    `work week` WITH
        `week total`      IS w's `week total` TIMES f
        `week frontal`    IS w's `week frontal` TIMES f
        `week individual` IS w's `week individual` TIMES f
        `week stay`       IS w's `week stay` TIMES f

-- 5.4: a teaching employee may work in no more than two schools (in the
-- reform or not), provided the total position across them is no more than
-- 100%; not for teaching employees of the health professions.
@ref akn:art_5__para_5-4
GIVEN `number of schools` IS A NUMBER, `total position` IS A NUMBER, `of the health professions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `5.4 permits the employment` `number of schools` `total position` `of the health professions` IF
    `of the health professions`
    OR (`number of schools` AT MOST 2 AND `total position` AT MOST 1)

§§ `6 העסקה מעל 100% משרה באופק חדש`

-- akn:art_6 The heading of section 6; no rule.

-- 6.1: as a rule up to 100%; above it only in exceptional cases, for
-- teaching employees (not principals or first deputies), by the system's
-- needs; the extra hours are frontal only; the total is at most 8.5 hours
-- a day and 42 a week.
@ref akn:art_6__para_6-1 akn:art_6__para_6-1/p2 akn:art_6__para_6-1/p3 akn:art_6__para_6-1/p4
GIVEN r IS A `role`, `an exceptional case the system needs` IS A BOOLEAN, `the extra hours are all frontal` IS A BOOLEAN, `daily hours` IS A NUMBER, `weekly hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be employed above 100%` r `an exceptional case the system needs` `the extra hours are all frontal` `daily hours` `weekly hours` IF
        `an exceptional case the system needs`
    AND NOT (r EQUALS `principal` OR r EQUALS `first deputy principal`)
    AND `the extra hours are all frontal`
    AND `daily hours` AT MOST 8.5
    AND `weekly hours` AT MOST 42

-- 6.2: in one institution the principal may approve up to 42 weekly hours
-- without a request in the entitlements system. 6.3: in two institutions,
-- up to 106% without approval. 6.4: above 106% in two institutions, a
-- request is filed.
@ref akn:art_6__para_6-2 akn:art_6__para_6-3 akn:art_6__para_6-4
DECLARE `approval for over-100% employment` IS ONE OF
    `the principal approves, no request`
    `no approval needed`
    `a request in the entitlements system`

GIVEN `number of institutions` IS A NUMBER, `total position` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `approval for over-100% employment`
DECIDE `the approval needed` `number of institutions` `total position` IS
    IF `number of institutions` EQUALS 1
    THEN `the principal approves, no request`
    ELSE IF `total position` AT MOST 1.06
         THEN `no approval needed`
         ELSE `a request in the entitlements system`

-- F-2023-24_tashpad_01-f: 5.4 caps two schools at 100% in total; 6.3 lets
-- two institutions go to 106% without approval and 6.4 above it on
-- request. The reading adopted: section 6 is the exception to 5.4's cap.
`5.4 and 6.3 disagree on 104% in two schools` MEANS
        NOT `5.4 permits the employment` 2 1.04 FALSE
    AND `the approval needed` 2 1.04 EQUALS `no approval needed`
#ASSERT `5.4 and 6.3 disagree on 104% in two schools`

-- akn:art_6/p1 A link to the procedure for employment above 100% in recognized unofficial education for תשפ"ד; no rule.

§§ `7 עו"ה אם`

-- akn:art_7 The heading of section 7; no rule.

-- 7.1: entitlement to a mother's position follows the takanon: a teaching
-- employee whose whole position is 79% or more.
@ref akn:art_7__para_7-1 akn:art_7__para_7-1/p2
GIVEN `position` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to a mother's position` `position` IF
    `position` AT LEAST 0.79

-- 7.2: a mother may cut one frontal hour and one stay hour from the reform's
-- regular week; the tables above show it.
@ref akn:art_7__para_7-2 akn:art_7__para_7-2/p2
`a mother's reduction` MEANS `hours reduction` WITH
    `frontal reduction`    IS 1
    `individual reduction` IS 0
    `stay reduction`       IS 1

@desc A weekly reduction of hours, by kind.
DECLARE `hours reduction` HAS
    `frontal reduction`    IS A NUMBER
    `individual reduction` IS A NUMBER
    `stay reduction`       IS A NUMBER

-- 7.3: after maternity leave, at 90% or more, for four months: one hour a
-- day (5 a week) off the stay hours (nursing hour), pay and position
-- unchanged; 7.2 does not apply in that period.
@ref akn:art_7__para_7-3
`a nursing reduction` MEANS `hours reduction` WITH
    `frontal reduction`    IS 0
    `individual reduction` IS 0
    `stay reduction`       IS 5

`the nursing period in months` MEANS 4

-- 7.4: such an employee at 79% to 90% gets the mother's part-time stay
-- reduction of 7.2. 7.5: never both.
-- F-2023-24_tashpad_01-g: at exactly 90% both 7.3 ("90% ומעלה") and 7.4
-- ("79% עד 90%") apply, and 7.5 forbids both. The reading adopted: 7.3
-- governs at 90%, the clause that says "and above"; 7.4 covers 79% to
-- under 90%.
@ref akn:art_7__para_7-4 akn:art_7__para_7-5
GIVEN `position` IS A NUMBER, `within four months of maternity leave` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `hours reduction`
DECIDE `the mother's reduction` `position` `within four months of maternity leave` IS
    IF `within four months of maternity leave` AND `position` AT LEAST 0.9
    THEN `a nursing reduction`
    ELSE IF `entitled to a mother's position` `position`
         THEN `a mother's reduction`
         ELSE `no reduction`

`no reduction` MEANS `hours reduction` WITH
    `frontal reduction`    IS 0
    `individual reduction` IS 0
    `stay reduction`       IS 0

GIVEN `position` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `hours reduction`
DECIDE `the reductions 7.3 and 7.4 give after maternity leave` `position` IS
    append (IF `position` AT LEAST 0.9 THEN LIST `a nursing reduction` ELSE EMPTY)
           (IF `position` AT LEAST 0.79 AND `position` AT MOST 0.9 THEN LIST `a mother's reduction` ELSE EMPTY)

`7.3 and 7.4 both take a 90% position` MEANS
    count (`the reductions 7.3 and 7.4 give after maternity leave` 0.9) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `7.3 and 7.4 both take a 90% position`

§§ `8 מורים הזכאים לשעות גיל`

-- akn:art_8 The heading of section 8; no rule.

-- 8.1: the age of eligibility is determined as before the reform (the
-- teacher's `age` field).
@ref akn:art_8__para_8-1
`age eligibility is determined as before the reform` MEANS TRUE

-- 8.2: existing and new teachers aged 50-55: 2 frontal hours off (for a
-- full position; part-time proportionally); the base becomes 34.
-- 8.3: existing teachers aged 55 and over: 3 frontal and 1 individual; the
-- base becomes 32. 8.4: new teachers aged 55 and over: 2 frontal only,
-- base 34, and no further cut after the one at 50. ¶2: the tables above.
-- F-2023-24_tashpad_01-h: an existing teacher aged 55 is in 8.2 ("50 – 55")
-- and in 8.3 ("55 ומעלה"). The reading adopted: 8.3 governs at 55.
@ref akn:art_8__para_8-2 akn:art_8__para_8-3 akn:art_8__para_8-3/p2 akn:art_8__para_8-4 akn:art_8__para_8-4/p2
GIVEN t IS A `tashpad 1 teacher`
GIVETH AN `age hours`
DECIDE `the age hours of` t IS
    IF t's `age` AT LEAST 55 AND `is an existing teaching employee` t
    THEN `age hours` 3 1 32
    ELSE IF t's `age` AT LEAST 50
         THEN `age hours` 2 0 34
         ELSE `age hours` 0 0 36

@desc The age reduction for a full position, and the position base it leaves.
DECLARE `age hours` HAS
    `age frontal reduction`    IS A NUMBER
    `age individual reduction` IS A NUMBER
    `position base`            IS A NUMBER

GIVEN t IS A `tashpad 1 teacher`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the frontal hours cut for age` t IS
    (`the age hours of` t)'s `age frontal reduction` TIMES min (t's `position fraction`) 1

GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `age hours`
DECIDE `the age rows an existing teacher falls in` `age` IS
    append (IF `age` AT LEAST 50 AND `age` AT MOST 55 THEN LIST (`age hours` 2 0 34) ELSE EMPTY)
           (IF `age` AT LEAST 55 THEN LIST (`age hours` 3 1 32) ELSE EMPTY)

`8.2 and 8.3 both take an existing teacher aged 55` MEANS
    count (`the age rows an existing teacher falls in` 55) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `8.2 and 8.3 both take an existing teacher aged 55`

§§ `9 מבנה שבוע העבודה למנהלים וסגנים ראשונים`

-- akn:art_9 The heading of section 9; no rule.

-- 9.1: a principal and a first deputy in a reform school are employed at
-- exactly 100%, 5 days a week. 9.2: the principal's week is 40 hours, of
-- which 6 to 9 are frontal, by the school's complexity level. 9.7: the
-- first deputy's week is 40 hours.
@ref akn:art_9__para_9-1 akn:art_9__para_9-2 akn:art_9__para_9-7
`the position of a principal or first deputy` MEANS 1
`the work days of a principal or first deputy` MEANS 5
`the principal's weekly hours` MEANS 40
`the fewest frontal hours a principal teaches` MEANS 6
`the most frontal hours a principal teaches` MEANS 9
`the first deputy's weekly hours` MEANS 40

-- 9.3-9.4: the complexity level — 8 levels by the school-management index
-- (classes, kinds of disability, stages) — sets the frontal hours and the
-- pay of the principal and first deputy.
@ref akn:art_9__para_9-3 akn:art_9__para_9-4
`the number of complexity levels` MEANS 8

-- 9.5-9.6: the level is computed in early May of the year before, from the
-- Ministry's data that month; for a new or growing school, in December of
-- the year itself, with the minimum level until then and retroactive
-- correction from the start of the year.
@ref akn:art_9__para_9-5 akn:art_9__para_9-6
GIVEN `existed in May of the year before` IS A BOOLEAN, `growing school` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `when the complexity level is computed` `existed in May of the year before` `growing school` IS
    IF `existed in May of the year before` AND NOT `growing school`
    THEN "early May of the previous school year"
    ELSE "December of the school year, with the minimum level until then and a retroactive update"

-- 9.6's table as printed: the principal's frontal hours by complexity level.
-- F-2023-24_tashpad_01-a: the table prints level 1 twice and no level 2
-- (the page itself, checked against the PDF). The reading adopted: level 2
-- teaches 9, as levels 1 and 3 do and as 9.2's range allows.
@ref akn:art_9__para_9-6/p2 akn:art_9__para_9-6/p3 akn:art_9__para_9-6/t1
`the principal's frontal hours table` MEANS
    LIST `complexity row` 1 9,
         `complexity row` 1 9,
         `complexity row` 3 9,
         `complexity row` 4 8,
         `complexity row` 5 8,
         `complexity row` 6 7,
         `complexity row` 7 7,
         `complexity row` 8 6

@desc One printed row of a complexity table: the level and the frontal hours.
DECLARE `complexity row` HAS
    `row level`         IS A NUMBER
    `row frontal hours` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `table` IS A LIST OF `complexity row`
      `level` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `the hours the table gives` `table` `level` IS
    map (GIVEN r YIELD r's `row frontal hours`) (filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `row level` EQUALS `level`) `table`)

`the principal's table has no row for level 2 and two for level 1` MEANS
        `the hours the table gives` `the principal's frontal hours table` 2 EQUALS EMPTY
    AND count (`the hours the table gives` `the principal's frontal hours table` 1) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the principal's table has no row for level 2 and two for level 1`

GIVEN `level` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the principal's frontal hours` `level` IS
    IF `level` EQUALS 2
    THEN 9
    ELSE CONSIDER `the hours the table gives` `the principal's frontal hours table` `level`
         WHEN h FOLLOWED BY rest THEN h
         OTHERWISE 0

-- Every level's hours lie in 9.2's range of 6 to 9.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN l YIELD `the principal's frontal hours` l AT LEAST `the fewest frontal hours a principal teaches` AND `the principal's frontal hours` l AT MOST `the most frontal hours a principal teaches`)
            (LIST 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8)

-- akn:art_9__para_9-6/p4 akn:art_9__para_9-6/p5 A link to how the complexity level is computed; no rule.

-- 9.7.1's table: a first deputy in a primary school teaches 18-21 frontal
-- hours by complexity level.
@ref akn:art_9__para_9-7__subpara_9-7-1 akn:art_9__para_9-7__subpara_9-7-1/t1
`the first deputy's frontal hours table` MEANS
    LIST `complexity row` 1 21,
         `complexity row` 2 21,
         `complexity row` 3 21,
         `complexity row` 4 21,
         `complexity row` 5 20,
         `complexity row` 6 20,
         `complexity row` 7 19,
         `complexity row` 8 18

#ASSERT all (GIVEN l YIELD count (`the hours the table gives` `the first deputy's frontal hours table` l) EQUALS 1)
            (LIST 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8)
#ASSERT all (GIVEN r YIELD r's `row frontal hours` AT LEAST 18 AND r's `row frontal hours` AT MOST 21) `the first deputy's frontal hours table`

-- 9.8: a second or later deputy works a teacher's week, the individual
-- hours going to the deputy's work.
@ref akn:art_9__para_9-8
`the week of a second or later deputy` MEANS `the primary teacher's week`

`a second or later deputy's individual hours go to` MEANS "work arising from the post of deputy"

-- 9.9: a principal or first deputy entitled to a mother's position gets 2
-- weekly hours off the non-frontal hours, position and pay unchanged.
-- 9.10: likewise at age 50 or more.
@ref akn:art_9__para_9-9 akn:art_9__para_9-10
GIVEN `entitled to a mother's position` IS A BOOLEAN, `age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `a manager's non-frontal reductions` `entitled to a mother's position` `age` IS
    append (IF `entitled to a mother's position` THEN LIST 2 ELSE EMPTY)
           (IF `age` AT LEAST 50 THEN LIST 2 ELSE EMPTY)

-- 9.11: an existing non-academic principal with 1 to 27 years of salary
-- seniority in a reform school is asked to complete an academic education
-- within 4 years of the school's move, to keep the post, and meanwhile is
-- employed on the non-academic principals' reform terms. 9.12: with 28
-- years or more, employed on those terms.
@ref akn:art_9__para_9-11 akn:art_9__para_9-12
GIVEN `salary seniority` IS A NUMBER, `years since the school moved` IS A NUMBER, `completed a degree` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a non-academic principal keeps the post` `salary seniority` `years since the school moved` `completed a degree` IF
    `salary seniority` AT LEAST 28
    OR `completed a degree`
    OR `years since the school moved` AT MOST 4

GIVEN `salary seniority` IS A NUMBER, `completed a degree` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `employed on the non-academic principals' reform terms` `salary seniority` `completed a degree` IF
    `salary seniority` AT LEAST 1 AND NOT `completed a degree`

-- 9.13: by section 31.1 of the agreement of 19.10.2022, the salary of
-- principals and first deputies is a global salary for all the work of the
-- post, whenever done.
@ref akn:art_9__para_9-13 akn:art_9__para_9-13/p2
GIVEN r IS A `role`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is paid a global salary` r IF
    r EQUALS `principal` OR r EQUALS `first deputy principal`

§§ `10 שעות פעילות בית ספרית`

-- akn:art_10 The heading of section 10; no rule.

DECLARE `school-activity hour` IS ONE OF
    `on the teacher's day off`
    `instead of a stay hour that day`
    `instead of a stay hour that is made up another day`

-- 10.1: a reform teacher (any position) is paid 125% of the hour value for
-- school activities, on top of position and pay. 10.5-10.7: on the day off,
-- 125%; instead of a stay hour, 125% and the stay hour's regular 100% is
-- not paid; instead of a stay hour made up another day, 125% and the 100%.
-- The rule gives what the activity hour adds to the teacher's pay.
@ref akn:art_10__para_10-1 akn:art_10__para_10-5 akn:art_10__para_10-6 akn:art_10__para_10-7
GIVEN h IS A `school-activity hour`, `hour value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the change in pay for a school-activity hour` h `hour value` IS
    CONSIDER h
    WHEN `on the teacher's day off` THEN 1.25 TIMES `hour value`
    WHEN `instead of a stay hour that day` THEN 1.25 TIMES `hour value` MINUS `hour value`
    WHEN `instead of a stay hour that is made up another day` THEN 1.25 TIMES `hour value`

-- 10.2: no more than 40 hours in the school year. 10.3: they include a
-- pre-opening meeting of post holders or with pupils, up to 3 hours.
-- 10.4: the activities (assemblies, parents' meetings, after-hours events),
-- allocated by the principal.
@ref akn:art_10__para_10-2 akn:art_10__para_10-3 akn:art_10__para_10-4
`the most school-activity hours in a year` MEANS 40
`the most pre-opening meeting hours` MEANS 3

GIVEN `hours allocated` IS A NUMBER, `pre-opening hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the allocation is within the limits` `hours allocated` `pre-opening hours` IF
        `hours allocated` AT MOST `the most school-activity hours in a year`
    AND `pre-opening hours` AT MOST `the most pre-opening meeting hours`
    AND `pre-opening hours` AT MOST `hours allocated`

§§ `11 יציאה מאופק חדש`

-- akn:art_11 The heading of section 11; no rule.

DECLARE `reason to leave` IS ONE OF
    `the health of the teacher or a first-degree relative, with current medical certificates`
    `a change for the worse in personal or family circumstances since joining`
    `another reason`

-- 11.1: as a rule every teacher who meets the joining conditions joins.
-- 11.2: in exceptional cases, and not for new teachers, a request to leave
-- may be considered for health or humanitarian reasons; a teacher whose
-- request is approved leaves.
@ref akn:art_11__para_11-1 akn:art_11__para_11-2 akn:art_11__para_11-2/p2 akn:art_11__para_11-2/p3 akn:art_11__para_11-2/p4 akn:art_11__para_11-2/p5
GIVEN t IS A `tashpad 1 teacher`, r IS A `reason to leave`, `the request was approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `stays in Ofek Hadash` t r `the request was approved` IF
        `joins Ofek Hadash` t
    AND NOT (`the request was approved` AND `a request to leave may be considered` t r)

GIVEN t IS A `tashpad 1 teacher`, r IS A `reason to leave`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a request to leave may be considered` t r IF
        NOT `is a new teaching employee` t
    AND NOT (r EQUALS `another reason`)

-- 11.3-11.4: the request is filed through the principal on annex ג's form,
-- by e-mail.
@ref akn:art_11__para_11-3 akn:art_11__para_11-4
`the form for a request to leave` MEANS "annex ג"

§§ `12 ותק בהוראה`

-- akn:art_12 The heading of section 12; no rule.

-- 12.1: recognized seniority for the salary table is teaching seniority as
-- the takanon defines it, without the internship and compulsory IDF
-- service, but with teaching in IDF or national service under the takanon.
@ref akn:art_12__para_12-1
GIVEN `takanon teaching seniority` IS A NUMBER, `internship years in it` IS A NUMBER, `compulsory service years in it` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `recognized seniority` `takanon teaching seniority` `internship years in it` `compulsory service years in it` IS
    `takanon teaching seniority` MINUS `internship years in it` MINUS `compulsory service years in it`

-- 12.2: "notwithstanding section 13.1", an existing teacher keeps every
-- year recognized for salary before moving to Ofek Hadash.
-- F-2023-24_tashpad_01-e: 13.1 is the promotion criteria; the rule 12.2
-- departs from is 12.1.
@ref akn:art_12__para_12-2
GIVEN `years recognized before the move` IS A NUMBER, `recognized seniority under 12.1` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `an existing teacher's recognized seniority` `years recognized before the move` `recognized seniority under 12.1` IS
    max `years recognized before the move` `recognized seniority under 12.1`

`the section 12.2 says it departs from` MEANS "13.1"
`the subject of section 13.1` MEANS "promotion criteria"
`12.2 departs from a section about something else` MEANS
    `the section 12.2 says it departs from` EQUALS "13.1" AND `the subject of section 13.1` EQUALS "promotion criteria"
#ASSERT `12.2 departs from a section about something else`

§§ `13 קידום בדרגות הערכה ופיתוח מקצועי`

-- akn:art_13 The heading of section 13; no rule.

-- 13.1: promotion from grade to grade requires the required period (פז"נ),
-- professional-development hours (שפ"מ) by the Ministry's outline, and an
-- evaluation by the Ministry's guidelines; links follow.
@ref akn:art_13__para_13-1 akn:art_13__para_13-1/p2 akn:art_13__para_13-1/p3 akn:art_13__para_13-1/p4
GIVEN `months in grade` IS A NUMBER, `development hours` IS A NUMBER, `evaluation passed` IS A BOOLEAN, s IS A `promotion step`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the promotion criteria` `months in grade` `development hours` `evaluation passed` s IF
        `months in grade` AT LEAST s's `required months`
    AND `development hours` AT LEAST s's `required hours`
    AND `evaluation passed`

-- akn:art_13__para_13-1/p5 akn:art_13__para_13-1/p6 akn:art_13__para_13-1/p7 akn:art_13__para_13-1/p8 akn:art_13__para_13-1/p9 Links to the evaluation for promotion and to the map of indicators; no rule.
-- akn:art_13__para_13-2 The heading of 13.2 (teachers' promotion); no rule.

@desc One printed row of a promotion table: from grade, to grade, the required months (פז"נ) and development hours (שפ"מ).
DECLARE `promotion step` HAS
    `from grade`      IS A STRING
    `to grade`        IS A STRING
    `required months` IS A NUMBER
    `required hours`  IS A NUMBER

-- 13.2.1's table: certified academics, teachers and kindergarten teachers.
@ref akn:art_13__para_13-2__subpara_13-2-1 akn:art_13__para_13-2__subpara_13-2-1/t1
`the certified academics' promotion table` MEANS
    LIST `promotion step` "1" "2" 30 120,
         `promotion step` "2" "3" 30 120,
         `promotion step` "3" "4" 36 180,
         `promotion step` "4" "5" 36 180,
         `promotion step` "5" "6" 36 180,
         `promotion step` "6" "7" 48 210,
         `promotion step` "7" "8" 48 210,
         `promotion step` "8" "9" 48 210

-- akn:art_13__para_13-2__subpara_13-2-2 The heading of 13.2.2 (academics not certified to teach); no rule.

-- 13.2.2: veteran teachers with "up to 25" years who join by exception may
-- not advance until certified; once certified, the period and hours count
-- from joining (for one promotion only) and up to 60 study hours count as
-- development hours. Those with "25 and more" years need not certify and
-- advance as certified academics. New teachers joining by exception may not
-- advance until certified, get none of the benefits, and accrue from
-- certification.
-- F-2023-24_tashpad_01-i: at exactly 25 years a teacher is in "עד 25" and in
-- "25 ומעלה". The reading adopted: 25 years is "25 and more" (as 3.2.1 bars
-- only seniority "below 25").
@ref akn:art_13__para_13-2__subpara_13-2-2/p2 akn:art_13__para_13-2__subpara_13-2-2/p3 akn:art_13__para_13-2__subpara_13-2-2/p4 akn:art_13__para_13-2__subpara_13-2-2/p5 akn:art_13__para_13-2__subpara_13-2-2/p6 akn:art_13__para_13-2__subpara_13-2-2/p7
GIVEN t IS A `tashpad 1 teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an uncertified academic may advance` t IF
    t's `certified to teach` OR (`is an existing teaching employee` t AND t's `teaching seniority` AT LEAST 25)

`the most study hours counted as development hours` MEANS 60

GIVEN `seniority` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF BOOLEAN
DECIDE `what 13.2.2's two rows say of advancing uncertified` `seniority` IS
    append (IF `seniority` AT MOST 25 THEN LIST FALSE ELSE EMPTY)
           (IF `seniority` AT LEAST 25 THEN LIST TRUE ELSE EMPTY)

`13.2.2 gives a teacher of exactly 25 years both answers` MEANS
    `what 13.2.2's two rows say of advancing uncertified` 25 EQUALS LIST FALSE, TRUE
#ASSERT `13.2.2 gives a teacher of exactly 25 years both answers`

-- akn:art_13__para_13-2__subpara_13-2-3 The heading of 13.2.3 (certified non-academics); no rule.

-- 13.2.3: certified non-academics with 28 years or more need not complete
-- an academic education; they advance by this table.
@ref akn:art_13__para_13-2__subpara_13-2-3/p2 akn:art_13__para_13-2__subpara_13-2-3/t1
`the certified non-academics' promotion table` MEANS
    LIST `promotion step` "1" "2" 48 480,
         `promotion step` "2" "3" 48 480,
         `promotion step` "3" "4" 48 480,
         `promotion step` "4" "5" 48 480,
         `promotion step` "5" "6" 48 480,
         `promotion step` "6" "7" 48 480,
         `promotion step` "7" "8" 48 480,
         `promotion step` "8" "9" 48 480

-- akn:art_13__para_13-3 The heading of 13.3 (principals' and deputies' promotion); no rule.

-- 13.3.1's table: certified academic principals and deputies.
@ref akn:art_13__para_13-3__subpara_13-3-1 akn:art_13__para_13-3__subpara_13-3-1/t1
`the academic managers' promotion table` MEANS
    LIST `promotion step` "א" "ב" 36 210,
         `promotion step` "ב" "ג" 36 210,
         `promotion step` "ג" "ד" 36 210

-- 13.3.2's table: certified non-academic principals and deputies with 28
-- years or more, who need not complete an academic education.
@ref akn:art_13__para_13-3__subpara_13-3-2 akn:art_13__para_13-3__subpara_13-3-2/t1
`the non-academic managers' promotion table` MEANS
    LIST `promotion step` "א" "ב" 48 480,
         `promotion step` "ב" "ג" 48 480,
         `promotion step` "ג" "ד" 48 480

#ASSERT `meets the promotion criteria` 30 120 TRUE (`promotion step` "1" "2" 30 120)
#ASSERT NOT `meets the promotion criteria` 47 480 TRUE (`promotion step` "1" "2" 48 480)

§§ `14 יועצים חינוכיים`

-- The counselors' section prints as a second "14", its paragraphs numbered
-- 13.1-13.3; the corpus files it under 13.3.2's keys. ¶2 is its heading.
-- akn:art_13__para_13-3__subpara_13-3-2/p2 The heading "14 יועצים חינוכיים" (educational counselors); no rule.

-- ¶3-¶11 (its "13.1"): a counselor works an academic teacher's week,
-- except that the frontal hours are split between teaching and counseling
-- as the principal decides, the individual hours are counseling, and the
-- stay hours serve the counseling too; at least 1/6 of the position (6 of
-- 36 for a full one) is frontal teaching in primary and junior-high
-- schools, and no less than 4 frontal hours for any position.
@ref akn:art_13__para_13-3__subpara_13-3-2/p3 akn:art_13__para_13-3__subpara_13-3-2/p4 akn:art_13__para_13-3__subpara_13-3-2/p5 akn:art_13__para_13-3__subpara_13-3-2/p6 akn:art_13__para_13-3__subpara_13-3-2/p7 akn:art_13__para_13-3__subpara_13-3-2/p8 akn:art_13__para_13-3__subpara_13-3-2/p9 akn:art_13__para_13-3__subpara_13-3-2/p10 akn:art_13__para_13-3__subpara_13-3-2/p11
GIVEN `position` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a counselor's minimum frontal teaching hours` `position` IS
    max (36 TIMES `position` DIVIDED BY 6) 4

-- ¶12 (its "13.2"): new counselors are paid by the new combined-salary
-- tables for academic teachers.
@ref akn:art_13__para_13-3__subpara_13-3-2/p12
`the table new counselors are paid by` MEANS "the new combined-salary tables for academic teachers"

-- ¶13-¶15 (its "13.3"): a counselor with at least 7 counseling hours earns
-- the counseling bonus: 12% with a temporary licence, 18% with a permanent
-- one.
@ref akn:art_13__para_13-3__subpara_13-3-2/p13 akn:art_13__para_13-3__subpara_13-3-2/p14 akn:art_13__para_13-3__subpara_13-3-2/p15
GIVEN `counseling hours` IS A NUMBER, `permanent licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the counseling bonus rate` `counseling hours` `permanent licence` IS
    IF `counseling hours` AT LEAST 7
    THEN IF `permanent licence` THEN 0.18 ELSE 0.12
    ELSE 0

§§ `14 קביעת הדרגה באופק חדש`

-- akn:art_14 The heading of section 14 (grade determination); no rule.

-- 14.1: the Ministry alone sets the grade. 14.2: from the employment,
-- education and salary data. 14.3: the Ministry's accountant converts by
-- the March salary of the year before joining (seniority, grade, training
-- credits, roles, and the conversion coefficient by status, as the
-- agreement details). 14.4: the salary for conversion is the salary (its
-- relevant components) the teacher was due at 100% by the roles held, in
-- March of the year before the move. 14.5: the grade may be a half grade.
-- The prohibition on the owner has no time limit.
@ref akn:art_14__para_14-1 akn:art_14__para_14-2 akn:art_14__para_14-3 akn:art_14__para_14-4 akn:art_14__para_14-5
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `tashpad 1 action`
DECIDE `only the Ministry sets grades` IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    SHANT `set the Ofek Hadash grade`
    LEST BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "circular תשפ\"ד/1 14.1: the Ministry of Education alone sets Ofek Hadash grades"

`the data the grade is set from` MEANS LIST "employment", "education", "salary"
`the salary month the conversion uses` MEANS "March of the year before the teacher joins the reform"
`the March data the conversion reads` MEANS
    LIST "seniority", "grade", "in-service training credits", "roles", "the conversion-coefficient supplement by status"
`the position the salary for conversion is taken at` MEANS 1

`grades step in halves` MEANS 0.5

-- akn:art_14__para_14-6 akn:art_14__para_14-6/p2 akn:art_14__para_14-6/p3 akn:art_14__para_14-6/p4 akn:art_14__para_14-6/p5 akn:art_14__para_14-6/p6 akn:art_14__para_14-6/p7 akn:art_14__para_14-6/p8 Pointers: more on conversions in the booklet, explanation and examples in annex ד (encoded below), and links to the salary tables and the 2016 shekel and Ofek 2022 supplement circulars; no rule.

-- akn:art_14__para_14-7 The heading "גמולי תפקיד באופק חדש" (role bonuses); no rule.

@desc One printed role bonus: the role and its rate of the combined salary.
DECLARE `role bonus` HAS
    `bonus role` IS A STRING
    `bonus rate` IS A NUMBER

-- 14.7 ¶2-¶16 as printed. The grade coordinator's 7%/6% is by the classes
-- in the grade (14.8.2); the mentor's 2.4% is per intern, for up to three;
-- the special-education bonus is set below.
@ref akn:art_14__para_14-7/p2 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p3 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p4 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p5 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p6 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p7 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p8 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p9 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p10 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p11 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p12 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p13 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p14 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p15 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p16
`the role bonuses` MEANS
    LIST `role bonus` "second deputy principal" 0.2,
         `role bonus` "class educator" 0.1,
         `role bonus` "first-grade class educator" 0.115,
         `role bonus` "subject coordinator, primary" 0.06,
         `role bonus` "road-safety coordinator" 0.06,
         `role bonus` "security coordinator" 0.06,
         `role bonus` "social education, primary" 0.08,
         `role bonus` "grade coordinator, up to 4 classes" 0.07,
         `role bonus` "grade coordinator, over 4 classes" 0.06,
         `role bonus` "laboratory coordinator" 0.03,
         `role bonus` "measurement and evaluation coordinator" 0.06,
         `role bonus` "trips coordinator" 0.06,
         `role bonus` "inclusion and integration coordinator" 0.06,
         `role bonus` "pedagogic coordinator" 0.08,
         `role bonus` "mentor, per intern" 0.024

`the most interns a mentor is paid for` MEANS 3

-- ¶17: the post holders are appointed by the Ministry's instructions.
-- ¶18: a teaching employee earns at most two role bonuses.
@ref akn:art_14__para_14-7/p17 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p18
GIVEN `rates of the roles held` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the role bonuses are within the limit` `rates of the roles held` IF
    count `rates of the roles held` AT MOST 2

`the post holders are appointed by` MEANS "the Ministry of Education's instructions"

-- ¶19-¶20: by the agreement of 19.10.2022, from 1.9.2023 the
-- special-education bonus of section 39א(3) of the Ofek Hadash agreement
-- rises as follows. For one certified in special education who meets the
-- bonus's conditions: 9% becomes 10%, 14% becomes 15%, and in a class the
-- Ministry defined as autism or severe mental disorders 17%. For one not
-- certified: 5.5%, and 8.5% in special education.
@ref akn:art_14__para_14-7/p19 akn:art_14__para_14-7/p20 akn:art_14__para_14-7__hc_1__subpara_a akn:art_14__para_14-7__hc_1__subpara_b akn:art_14__para_14-7__hc_1__subpara_c akn:art_14__para_14-7__hc_2__subpara_a akn:art_14__para_14-7__hc_2__subpara_b
GIVEN `certified in special education` IS A BOOLEAN, `rate before the agreement` IS A NUMBER, `autism or severe mental disorders class` IS A BOOLEAN, `in special education` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the special-education bonus from 1.9.2023` `certified in special education` `rate before the agreement` `autism or severe mental disorders class` `in special education` IS
    IF `certified in special education`
    THEN IF `rate before the agreement` EQUALS 0.14 AND `autism or severe mental disorders class`
         THEN 0.17
         ELSE IF `rate before the agreement` EQUALS 0.14
              THEN 0.15
              ELSE IF `rate before the agreement` EQUALS 0.09 THEN 0.1 ELSE `rate before the agreement`
    ELSE IF `in special education` THEN 0.085 ELSE 0.055

-- akn:art_14__para_14-7__hc_1 The lead-in for a teaching employee certified in special education; no rule of its own.
-- akn:art_14__para_14-7__hc_2 The lead-in for a teaching employee not certified in special education; no rule of its own.

-- 14.8: minimum shekel amounts. 14.8.1 class educator: the higher of 10%
-- (11.5% in first grade) of the combined salary and 1,000. 14.8.2 grade
-- coordinator and 14.8.3 head of the young division: the higher of 7% (up
-- to 4 classes in the grade) or 6% (more) and 1,100. 14.8.4 deputy: the
-- higher of 20% and 1,100.
@ref akn:art_14__para_14-8 akn:art_14__para_14-8__subpara_14-8-1 akn:art_14__para_14-8__subpara_14-8-1/p2 akn:art_14__para_14-8__subpara_14-8-1/p3
GIVEN `combined salary` IS A NUMBER, `first grade` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the class educator's bonus` `combined salary` `first grade` IS
    max ((IF `first grade` THEN 0.115 ELSE 0.1) TIMES `combined salary`) 1000

@ref akn:art_14__para_14-8__subpara_14-8-2 akn:art_14__para_14-8__subpara_14-8-2/p2 akn:art_14__para_14-8__subpara_14-8-2/p3 akn:art_14__para_14-8__subpara_14-8-2/p4 akn:art_14__para_14-8__subpara_14-8-3 akn:art_14__para_14-8__subpara_14-8-3/p2 akn:art_14__para_14-8__subpara_14-8-3/p3 akn:art_14__para_14-8__subpara_14-8-3/p4
GIVEN `combined salary` IS A NUMBER, `classes in the grade` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the grade coordinator's or young-division head's bonus` `combined salary` `classes in the grade` IS
    max ((IF `classes in the grade` AT MOST 4 THEN 0.07 ELSE 0.06) TIMES `combined salary`) 1100

@ref akn:art_14__para_14-8__subpara_14-8-4 akn:art_14__para_14-8__subpara_14-8-4/p2 akn:art_14__para_14-8__subpara_14-8-4/p3
GIVEN `combined salary` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the deputy's bonus` `combined salary` IS
    max (0.2 TIMES `combined salary`) 1100

§§ `15 גמול ליווי טיולים`

-- akn:art_15 The heading of section 15; no rule.

-- 15.1: paid under the agreement of 8.9.98, but only for hours beyond the
-- working hours of section 4.
@ref akn:art_15__para_15-1
GIVEN `activity hours` IS A NUMBER, `of them within working hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `hours the escort bonus is paid for` `activity hours` `of them within working hours` IS
    max (`activity hours` MINUS `of them within working hours`) 0

-- 15.2's table as printed, for an activity that ends: by 15:00, 0; 15:00-
-- 16:00, 0.5; 16:00-18:00, 1.5; 18:00-21:00, 3; 21:00-24:00, 4.5. A
-- detached activity 16:00-24:00, 3; with an overnight stay, 6.5.
@ref akn:art_15__para_15-2 akn:art_15__para_15-2/p2 akn:art_15__para_15-2__subpara_a akn:art_15__para_15-2__subpara_a/p2 akn:art_15__para_15-2__subpara_a/p3 akn:art_15__para_15-2__subpara_a/p4 akn:art_15__para_15-2__subpara_a/p5 akn:art_15__para_15-2__subpara_a/p6
`the escort table by ending hour` MEANS
    LIST `escort band` 0  15 0,
         `escort band` 15 16 0.5,
         `escort band` 16 18 1.5,
         `escort band` 18 21 3,
         `escort band` 21 24 4.5

@desc One printed row of 15.2's table: when the activity ends (in hours of the day), or its kind, and the bonus units.
DECLARE `escort band` HAS
    `band from hour` IS A NUMBER
    `band to hour`   IS A NUMBER
    `band units`     IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `ending hour` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `the units the table gives for an end at` `ending hour` IS
    map (GIVEN b YIELD b's `band units`)
        (filter (GIVEN b YIELD `ending hour` AT LEAST b's `band from hour` AND `ending hour` AT MOST b's `band to hour`)
                `the escort table by ending hour`)

-- F-2023-24_tashpad_01-j: an activity ending exactly at 16:00, 18:00 or
-- 21:00 is in two rows. The reading adopted: a row's end hour belongs to
-- it ("עד 15:00" includes 15:00), so a band runs from after its first hour
-- to its last.
`the escort table gives an end at 16:00 two unit counts` MEANS
    `the units the table gives for an end at` 16 EQUALS LIST 0.5, 1.5
#ASSERT `the escort table gives an end at 16:00 two unit counts`

GIVEN `ending hour` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `escort units for an end at` `ending hour` IS
    BRANCH IF `ending hour` AT MOST 15 THEN 0
           IF `ending hour` AT MOST 16 THEN 0.5
           IF `ending hour` AT MOST 18 THEN 1.5
           IF `ending hour` AT MOST 21 THEN 3
           OTHERWISE 4.5

@ref akn:art_15__para_15-2__subpara_b akn:art_15__para_15-2__subpara_b/p2
`the units of a detached activity between 16:00 and 24:00` MEANS 3

@ref akn:art_15__para_15-2__subpara_c
`the units of an activity with an overnight stay` MEANS 6.5

-- 15.3: a unit is worth 0.7% of the monthly combined salary of a full
-- position (not by the teacher's position).
@ref akn:art_15__para_15-3
GIVEN `units` IS A NUMBER, `full-position combined salary` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the escort bonus` `units` `full-position combined salary` IS
    `units` TIMES 0.007 TIMES `full-position combined salary`

-- 15.4: escorting on the day off, or on a day of fewer than 7 hours, is
-- paid in hours at the reform's substitute-hour value: placed for 0 hours,
-- 7 hours; for 1, 6; ... for 6, 1; for 7 or more, 0 — or the activity's
-- hours if fewer.
-- F-2023-24_tashpad_01-k: 15.4 does not say whether these hours replace the
-- units of 15.2 or come on top of them. The reading adopted: on such a day
-- 15.4 governs and the units are not paid as well.
@ref akn:art_15__para_15-4 akn:art_15__para_15-4/p2 akn:art_15__para_15-4/p3 akn:art_15__para_15-4/p4 akn:art_15__para_15-4/p5 akn:art_15__para_15-4/p6 akn:art_15__para_15-4/p7 akn:art_15__para_15-4/p8 akn:art_15__para_15-4/p9 akn:art_15__para_15-4/p10 akn:art_15__para_15-4/p11 akn:art_15__para_15-4/p12 akn:art_15__para_15-4/p13 akn:art_15__para_15-4/p14 akn:art_15__para_15-4/p15 akn:art_15__para_15-4/p16 akn:art_15__para_15-4/p17
GIVEN `hours placed that day` IS A NUMBER, `activity hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `substitute hours paid for escorting` `hours placed that day` `activity hours` IS
    min (max (7 MINUS `hours placed that day`) 0) `activity hours`

GIVEN `hours placed that day` IS A NUMBER, `ending hour` IS A NUMBER, `activity hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `the payments 15.2 and 15.4 name for one escort` `hours placed that day` `ending hour` `activity hours` IS
    LIST (`escort units for an end at` `ending hour`),
         (IF `hours placed that day` LESS THAN 7 THEN `substitute hours paid for escorting` `hours placed that day` `activity hours` ELSE 0)

`a short-day escort ending at 20:00 is named both units and hours` MEANS
    all (GIVEN x YIELD x GREATER THAN 0) (`the payments 15.2 and 15.4 name for one escort` 3 20 9)
#ASSERT `a short-day escort ending at 20:00 is named both units and hours`

§§ `16 מקדמות שכר באופק חדש עד לקביעת הדרגה`

-- akn:art_16 The heading of section 16; no rule.

@desc The current (non-reform) salary components 16.1 computes the advance on, for one month.
DECLARE `advance components` HAS
    `combined salary component`   IS A NUMBER
    `supplement 87`               IS A NUMBER
    `supplement 94`               IS A NUMBER
    `supplement 2001`             IS A NUMBER
    `supplement 2008`             IS A NUMBER
    `split-day bonus`             IS A NUMBER
    `in-service training bonuses` IS A NUMBER
    `double-degree bonus`         IS A NUMBER
    `supplement 2011`             IS A NUMBER

GIVEN c IS AN `advance components`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the advance base` c IS
    c's `combined salary component`
    PLUS c's `supplement 87`
    PLUS c's `supplement 94`
    PLUS c's `supplement 2001`
    PLUS c's `supplement 2008`
    PLUS c's `split-day bonus`
    PLUS c's `in-service training bonuses`
    PLUS c's `double-degree bonus`
    PLUS c's `supplement 2011`

-- 16.2: the advance rate: 14% for academics who are not principals or first
-- deputies; for academic managers, 17% for first deputies and 12% for
-- principals.
-- F-2023-24_tashpad_01-l: no rate is set for a non-academic — a teacher with
-- 28 years (3.3.1) or a principal (9.11-9.12), both employed on the reform's
-- terms. The reading adopted: none is paid under this circular until the
-- grade is set; the encoding returns no rate.
@ref akn:art_16__para_16-2 akn:art_16__para_16-2/p2 akn:art_16__para_16-2/p3 akn:art_16__para_16-2/p4 akn:art_16__para_16-2/p5
GIVEN r IS A `role`, `academic` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the advance rate` r `academic` IS
    IF NOT `academic`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER r
         WHEN `principal` THEN JUST 0.12
         WHEN `first deputy principal` THEN JUST 0.17
         OTHERWISE JUST 0.14

`16.2 sets no advance rate for a non-academic` MEANS
    isNothing (`the advance rate` `teacher` FALSE) AND isNothing (`the advance rate` `principal` FALSE)
#ASSERT `16.2 sets no advance rate for a non-academic`

-- 16.1: until the grade is set, the owner pays the joined teachers an
-- advance ("מקדמת אופק חדש") on top of their current salary, computed on
-- that salary's listed components, only for the part of the position in
-- the joined school and from the joining date; when the grade is set, pay
-- is recomputed back to joining and what was paid, the advance included,
-- is offset.
@ref akn:art_16__para_16-1 akn:art_16__para_16-1/p2 akn:art_16__para_16-1/p3 akn:art_16__para_16-1/p4
GIVEN r IS A `role`, `academic` IS A BOOLEAN, c IS AN `advance components`, `share in the joined school` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the Ofek Hadash advance` r `academic` c `share in the joined school` IS
    CONSIDER `the advance rate` r `academic`
    WHEN JUST rate THEN rate TIMES `the advance base` c TIMES `share in the joined school`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 0

-- The owner computes the advance for each teacher and pays it; the text
-- sets no deadline beyond "until the grade is set".
GIVEN r IS A `role`, `academic` IS A BOOLEAN, c IS AN `advance components`, `share in the joined school` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `tashpad 1 action`
DECIDE `payment of the Ofek Hadash advance` r `academic` c `share in the joined school` IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    MUST  `pay the Ofek Hadash advance` `amount paid`
          PROVIDED `amount paid` AT LEAST `the Ofek Hadash advance` r `academic` c `share in the joined school`
    LEST BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "circular תשפ\"ד/1 16.1: until the grade is set, the owner pays the joined teachers the Ofek Hadash advance"

GIVEN `paid before the grade was set` IS A NUMBER, `due on the set grade` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the retroactive difference` `paid before the grade was set` `due on the set grade` IS
    `due on the set grade` MINUS `paid before the grade was set`

§§ `17 שעון הנוכחות בביה"ס`

-- akn:art_17 The heading of section 17; no rule.

-- 17.1: an attendance clock is installed and teachers report their hours
-- by it. 17.3: until it is, reporting is by hand. The text sets no
-- deadline.
@ref akn:art_17__para_17-1 akn:art_17__para_17-3
GIVEN `the clock is installed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `tashpad 1 action`
DECIDE `the attendance clock` `the clock is installed` IS
    (PARTY `the local authority or owning body` MUST `install an attendance clock`)
    RAND
    (IF `the clock is installed`
     THEN PARTY `the teaching employee` MUST `report hours by the attendance clock`
     ELSE PARTY `the teaching employee` MUST `report hours by hand`)

-- 17.2: hours count from clocking in, and not before 7:45.
@ref akn:art_17__para_17-2
GIVEN `clock-in time` IS A NUMBER @desc in hours of the day, 7.75 is 7:45
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `hours count from` `clock-in time` IS
    max `clock-in time` 7.75

-- 17.4: the owner must pay and deduct by the clock's reports, after
-- checking approvals of justified absence (sickness, mourning and the like).
@ref akn:art_17__para_17-4
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `tashpad 1 action`
DECIDE `pay by the attendance reports` IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    MUST  `pay and deduct by the attendance reports`
    LEST BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "circular תשפ\"ד/1 17.4: the owner pays and deducts by the attendance clock's reports"

-- ¶1 (printed "18"): the circular gathers the agreements' rules; where it
-- and the agreements conflict, for or against the employee, the agreements
-- govern.
@ref akn:art_17/p1
GIVEN `the circular and the agreements conflict` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `source`
DECIDE `which governs` `the circular and the agreements conflict` IS
    IF `the circular and the agreements conflict` THEN `the collective agreements` ELSE `this circular`

DECLARE `source` IS ONE OF
    `this circular`
    `the collective agreements`

-- akn:art_17/p2 ("19") A pointer to the addresses in annex ה for more information; no rule.

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off, the signatories and the list of copies; no rule.

§§ `נספח א' — כתב התחייבות`

-- annex א ¶1-¶8: the owner's authorized signatory declares that every
-- payment the owner owes has been made (pension, study and severance funds,
-- salary paid on time), commits from תשפ"ד to apply to the teachers of its
-- listed schools all the Ofek Hadash agreement's provisions that concern a
-- school (work week, pay, pedagogic guidance), knows that breach may bring
-- sanctions up to revocation of the licence, and lists the schools.
@ref akn:att_1__hc_1/p1 akn:att_1__hc_1/p2 akn:att_1__hc_1/p3 akn:att_1__hc_1/p4 akn:att_1__hc_1/p5 akn:att_1__hc_1/p6 akn:att_1__hc_1/p7 akn:att_1__hc_1/p8
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `tashpad 1 action`
DECIDE `the owner's commitment` IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    MUST  `apply the Ofek Hadash agreement`
    WITHIN `1 September 2023`
    LEST BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "annex א: breach of the commitment may bring sanctions up to revocation of the licence"

-- akn:att_1__hc_1/p9 akn:att_1__hc_1/p10 akn:att_1__hc_1/p11 akn:att_1__hc_1/p12 akn:att_1__hc_1/p13 akn:att_1__hc_1/p14 akn:att_1__hc_1/p15 akn:att_1__hc_1/p16 The signature block and date lines of the commitment, and the next page's letterhead; no rule.

§§ `נספחים ב'-ג' — טפסים`

-- akn:att_2__hc_1 Annex ב, the form for an existing academic teacher without a teaching certificate to join by exception: the employee's and institution's details, the year, and the acknowledgements that 3.2.1 and 13.2.2 encode (no promotion until certified; the reform's terms apply on signing); sent by e-mail. No rule of its own.
-- akn:att_3__hc_1 Annex ג, the form for a request to the exceptions committee to leave Ofek Hadash: the employee's and institution's details, the request and the principal's comment; sent by e-mail (section 11 encodes the rule). No rule of its own.

§§ `נספח ד' — קביעת דרגה והמרות שכר`

-- ¶1-¶5: an existing teacher's grade is set by converting the salary, by
-- personal data, roles and the stage taught before joining; a new teacher
-- is placed at grade 1 by education and role without conversion; the
-- Ministry alone sets the grades (as 14.1).
@ref akn:att_4__hc_1/p1 akn:att_4__hc_1/p2 akn:att_4__hc_1/p3 akn:att_4__hc_1/p4 akn:att_4__hc_1/p5
GIVEN t IS A `tashpad 1 teacher`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the salary is converted` t IF
    `is an existing teaching employee` t

-- 1א, 2א, 3א: the conversion formula, A = X × (100 + Y) / 100, where X is
-- the salary for conversion, Y the conversion coefficient (in percent) and
-- A the salary after conversion.
@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_a akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_a/p2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_a/p3 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_a/p4 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_a/p5 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_a/p6
GIVEN X IS A NUMBER, Y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the salary after conversion by the formula` X Y IS
    X TIMES (100 PLUS Y) DIVIDED BY 100

-- The examples multiply X by the 3.4% erosion supplement first.
-- F-2023-24_tashpad_01-m: the formula has no erosion supplement; every
-- worked example applies one. The reading adopted: the examples' method.
GIVEN X IS A NUMBER, Y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the salary after conversion as the examples compute it` X Y IS
    X TIMES (1 PLUS `the erosion supplement`) TIMES (100 PLUS Y) DIVIDED BY 100

-- The erosion supplement the worked examples multiply by.
`the erosion supplement` MEANS 0.034

-- 1ב: X for a teacher — what the teacher would have been due at 100% by the
-- roles held in March of the year before the move, for: the combined
-- salary, supplements '87, '94, 2001, 2008 and 2011, and the role bonuses
-- that do not survive the reform (split day, training, in-service
-- training, double degree); with no employment in that March, the month of
-- joining.
@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p3 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p4 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p5 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p6
GIVEN `components at 100% in March` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a teacher's salary for conversion` `components at 100% in March` IS
    sum `components at 100% in March`

-- akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p7 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p8 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p9 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p10 The next page's letterhead; no rule.

-- ¶11-¶14: the academic teachers' coefficients — the page prints them as a
-- table (an image) that the corpus does not carry (a corpus defect), so
-- the academic coefficient is an input; non-academics (28 years and more)
-- take the academic coefficient times 0.8; for a primary teacher of grades
-- 7-9 on a 24-hour base the coefficient "grows by 12.5%" for that part of
-- the position.
-- F-2023-24_tashpad_01-o: "יגדל ב-12.5%" reads as 12.5% of the coefficient
-- or as 12.5 percentage points. The reading adopted: 12.5 points, the
-- reading in which "%" is the coefficient's own unit.
@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p11 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p12 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p13 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_b/p14
GIVEN `academic coefficient` IS A NUMBER @desc Y for an academic teacher of this status, in percent, from the page's table of academic coefficients (not in the corpus)
      `academic`             IS A BOOLEAN
      `grades 7-9 on a 24-hour base` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the conversion coefficient` `academic coefficient` `academic` `grades 7-9 on a 24-hour base` IS
    (IF `academic` THEN `academic coefficient` ELSE `academic coefficient` TIMES 0.8)
    PLUS (IF `grades 7-9 on a 24-hour base` THEN 12.5 ELSE 0)

GIVEN `academic coefficient` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the coefficient grown by 12.5% of itself` `academic coefficient` IS
    `academic coefficient` TIMES 1.125

`the two readings of 12.5% differ` MEANS
    NOT (`the conversion coefficient` 24 TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the coefficient grown by 12.5% of itself` 24)
#ASSERT `the two readings of 12.5% differ`

-- The teacher example (¶15-¶29, 1ג, 1ד ¶2-¶3): a mother, academic with a
