-- 1ד ¶2-¶3: an academic teacher is placed in the academic table by total
-- seniority, at the grade whose salary is closest to A and not below it;
-- here 10,967.27, grade 5.5.
@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_d akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_d/p2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_d/p3
GIVEN `A` IS A NUMBER, `salaries of the grades at this seniority` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the placed salary` `A` `salaries of the grades at this seniority` IS
    minimum (filter (GIVEN s YIELD s AT LEAST `A`) `salaries of the grades at this seniority`)

#ASSERT `the placed salary` `the teacher example's A as printed` (LIST 10500, 10967.27, 11400) EQUALS 10967.27

-- 1ד ¶4 and its points 1-3: new academics (after the internship) start at
-- grade 1, seniority 1, without conversion; a teacher on unpaid leave or
-- sabbatical or other unpaid absence in the year before joining is
-- converted on the salary due for September of the year of the move; the
-- 2016 shekel and Ofek 2022 supplements are due on top, by grade and rules.
@ref akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_d/p4 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_d__cls_1 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_d__cls_2 akn:att_4__hc_1__para_1__subpara_d__cls_3
GIVEN `absent without pay in the year before joining` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `the month the conversion salary is taken from` `absent without pay in the year before joining` IS
    IF `absent without pay in the year before joining`
    THEN "September of the year of the move"
    ELSE "March of the year before the move"

`a new academic's starting grade and seniority, without conversion` MEANS
    LIST `the starting grade of a new academic`, `the starting seniority of a new academic`

`the supplements due on top of the table salary` MEANS
    LIST "the 2016 shekel supplement", "the Ofek 2022 supplement"

